GCC-14 and Clang-19 each compile and execute the fixture at -std=c89
-O0 and -O2: 4/4 exit 0. For c89 and c90 both accept declarations named
inline, restrict, asm and typeof. In gnu89 both accept restrict as a name
and reject the other three name declarations (24 compile observations).
GCC rejects -std=c89 -fno-gnu89-inline; Clang accepts it. The existing
legacy-inline conflict policy refuses that final effective combination.

